        "notes": {
            "checkpoint": [
                "Starts on B1F (34, 29) where 13.02 ends. Ends below the second statue (27, 5), at (27, 6), with the flag set: (12, 10-12) is the opening the walk to the SECRET KEY takes.",
                "Barriers: Switch model (pokefirered data/scripts/pokemon_mansion.inc, PokemonMansion_*F scripts.inc; one global flag, set on a press and applied on each floor's load; the pack's maps are the flag-clear state only). Assumed per floor, to check against the overlay data: 1F set: (22-24,10-11), (27-29,25-26), (32-34,25-26) open, (31-33,18-19) closed. 2F set: (24-26,14-15), (10,30-32) open, (12,4-8) closed, (10,28-29) wall. 3F set: (17-19,11-12) open, (21,4-8) closed. B1F set: (12,10-12), (20-22,22-23) open, (33-35,20-21) and (16,28-30) closed. Clear = the map as it is.",
                "The two B1F statues are (24, 29) (press from (24, 30)) and (27, 5) (from (27, 6)). B1F is entered in the set state whichever way it was left, so the first press is a reset to clear: that opens the north, which the set state closes ((33-35, 20-21), (16, 28-30) are open in the clear state). The path to the Elixir and TM14 is the clear state, as the map is.",
                "Open: Burglar Lewis (wandering (19-21, 24-26), sight 1: Growlithe, Ponyta Lv34) cannot be avoided in the room; the row relies on the normal battle code if he fights. Ivan (34, 13, looking south, sight 6) is passed on x 33. The Elixir is a hidden item: the walk faces it from (34, 5).",
                "PokeGuy (1:19:56 to 1:20:21): basement statue, the Elixir 1:20:06, another statue 1:20:09, TM14 1:20:15."
            ]
        }
